{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '262,290p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/writer.cljc\nrg -n -A 42 'deftest bare-link-path' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/writer_test.cljc\nsed -n '410,438p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/writer.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"  \"The write `entry` (at `path`) woken by the append `outcome`, through\n   the engine's public applies: a program put's continuation by\n   `apply-put`, a retained FFI request's by `apply-ffi-outcome`, a link\n   request's by `apply-link-sent`.\"\n  [machine path entry outcome]\n  (let [m (get-in machine path)\n        applied (cond\n                  (= :link-request (:reason entry))\n                  (case (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)\n                    :dao.stream/ok\n                    (engine/apply-link-sent m (:link-id entry))\n                    :dao.stream/full\n                    m\n                    ;; the ungated append-link-request's own disposition:\n                    ;; a terminal outcome is a failure naming the link,\n                    ;; never a retryable wait\n                    (throw (ex-info \"Link request could not be appended\"\n                                    {:outcome (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)\n                                     :link-id (:link-id entry)})))\n                  (some? (call-id entry))\n                  (engine/apply-ffi-outcome m (call-id entry) outcome)\n                  :else\n                  (engine/apply-put m entry outcome))]\n    (if (seq path) (assoc-in machine path applied) applied)))\n\n\n(defn emit\n  \"One write step over `machine`, a task under custody: assign every\n   eligible enrolled write as one step, then perform every write the\n1071:(deftest bare-link-path-test\n1072-  (let [w (world)\n1073-        m0 (s/parked-linker)\n1074-        lid (:link-id (first (:wait-set m0)))\n1075-        m2 (engine/apply-link-cursor m0 lid 123)\n1076-        ;; At-least-once target so it goes through bare link path\n1077-        m-custody (assoc m2 :yin.k/custody\n1078-                         {:protection {(stream-id (get (:resources m2)\n1079-                                                       module/link-request-resource))\n1080-                                       :at-least-once}}\n1081-                         :yin.k/gate :running)\n1082-        h (get (:resources m-custody) yin.vm.module/link-request-resource)]\n1083-    (testing \"successful append transitions\"\n1084-      (let [r (writer/emit m-custody (appender w))]\n1085-        (is (= :link-response (:reason (first (:wait-set (:machine r))))))))\n1086-    (testing \"a terminal bare outcome is a failure naming the link, and the write is not retried\"\n1087-      (stream/close! h)\n1088-      (is (throws? #(writer/emit m-custody (appender w)))\n1089-          \"the closed stream's append answers closed: terminal, thrown\")\n1090-      (let [entry (first (:wait-set m-custody))]\n1091-        (is (= :link-request (:reason entry)))\n1092-        (is (not (contains? entry :op-id)) \"a bare write takes no id\")\n1093-        (is (some? (:envelope entry)) \"the envelope is retained verbatim\")))))\n1094-\n1095-\n1096-(deftest close-at-least-once-order-test\n1097-  (let [w (world)\n1098-        m0 (s/new-machine)\n1099-        h (log)\n1100-        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 h)\n1101-        m (assoc m1 :store {'w ref} :yin.k/gate :running)\n1102-        r1 (engine/handle-effect m (module/make-effect :stream/close {:stream ref}) gate-opts)\n1103-        r2 (engine/handle-effect (:state r1) (module/make-effect :stream/put {:stream ref, :val \"v2\"}) gate-opts)\n1104-        m-custody (assoc (:state r2) :yin.k/custody {:protection {(:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor h)) :at-least-once}})\n1105-        r (writer/emit m-custody (appender w))]\n1106-    (testing \"subsequent write sees :closed from earlier close\"\n1107-      (is (= 1 (count (:bare r))))\n1108-      (is (= :dao.stream/closed (:dao.stream/outcome (:outcome (first (:bare r))))))\n1109-      (is (empty? (:wait-set (:machine r))) \"the closed outcome woke the write off the wait set\")\n1110-      (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n1111-             (some-> (:ready-queue (:machine r)) first :status))\n1112-          \"woken with the closed status\"))))\n1113-\n\n\n(defn- retained\n  [machine reason]\n  {:machine machine ::retain reason})\n\n\n(defn- settle\n  \"The matched admission `answer` of `entry` (at `path`): an\n   authenticated `:committed` or `:replayed` applies the recorded effect\n   result; `:intent-conflict` ends the run with the occurrence\n   quarantined; `:stale` ends it with the tenure lost.  The entry keeps\n   its id through `:suspended`.\"\n  [machine path entry answer]\n  (case (get answer :yin.k/admission)\n    (:committed :replayed)\n    {:machine (apply-effect machine path entry\n                            (get answer :yin.k/effect-result))\n     :discharged {:path path\n                  :op-id (:op-id entry)\n                  :admission (get answer :yin.k/admission)\n                  :effect-result (get answer :yin.k/effect-result)}}\n    :intent-conflict\n    {:machine (ended machine)\n     :run-end {:cause :intent-conflict :op-id (:op-id entry)}}\n    :stale\n    {:machine (ended machine)\n     :run-end {:cause :stale :op-id (:op-id entry)}}\n    :suspended (retained machine :suspended)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-06 12:00:17 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 19:00:17 +0700\n\nSIGN-OFF (ready to land)\n\nThe shared link-outcome path now matches the existing protocol: `:ok` transitions, `:full` retains, and terminal outcomes throw with the outcome and link ID. Recorded admission results use that same path, so terminal failures cannot return a false successful discharge. The revised bare-link regression asserts terminal failure and preserves the envelope without assigning an ID. Earlier corrections remain intact; cross-host landing checks remain required. No files were edited and no suites were run."}}
